# civil-holidays v1
# jurisdiction: XNYS
# source: https://web.archive.org/web/20240118104341/https://www.nyse.com/publicdocs/nyse/regulation/nyse/NYSE_Rules.pdf
#   Structure and dates derived from vacanza/holidays 0.101 (MIT)
#   (github.com/vacanza/holidays), financial.ny_stock_exchange -- an
#   independent open-source reference maintained against the NYSE's own
#   published trading-calendar rules.
#   XNYS is a FINANCIAL MARKET jurisdiction, not an ISO-3166-1 country: it is
#   the New York Stock Exchange's trading-holiday calendar. English is
#   correct as the primary name here -- the NYSE publishes its calendar in
#   English, and the calendar belongs to an exchange, not a country with its
#   own official language.
#   Observed-shift is the same 5 U.S.C. 6103 rule already used for US.tab:
#   Saturday observed the preceding Friday, Sunday observed the following
#   Monday (the `us` policy). vacanza also registers this same calendar under
#   the short code NYSE; chronologia.civil_holidays.MARKET_ALIASES resolves
#   it onto this XNYS file rather than shipping a duplicate copy.
#   Every rule verified against vacanza 0.101 output for 2024, 2025 and 2026
#   (2026 exercises the `us` observed shift: 4 Jul 2026 is a Saturday, so
#   Independence Day is observed Fri 3 Jul 2026).
# retrieved: 2026-07-22
# categories: public|regional|municipal|religious|school
# columns: kind | name | args | categories | subdiv | observed | valid | span
#
fixed       | New Year's Day                       | 1 1    | public          | | us |      |
nth_weekday | Martin Luther King Jr. Day            | 1 3 0  | public          | |    |      |
nth_weekday | Washington's Birthday                 | 2 3 0  | public          | |    |      |
easter      | Good Friday                           | -2     | public religious | |  |      |
nth_weekday | Memorial Day                          | 5 -1 0 | public          | |    |      |
fixed       | Juneteenth National Independence Day  | 6 19   | public          | | us | 2022- |
fixed       | Independence Day                      | 7 4    | public          | | us |      |
nth_weekday | Labor Day                             | 9 1 0  | public          | |    |      |
nth_weekday | Thanksgiving Day                      | 11 4 3 | public          | |    |      |
fixed       | Christmas Day                         | 12 25  | public religious | | us |      |
